00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:09.570
Where'd that come from?

474
00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:10.750
And he's like, you know what?

475
00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:12.010
From my grandfather.

476
00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:14.210
He gave it to me when he died.

477
00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:15.690
And she said, well, I haven't seen it before.

478
00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:17.050
He must have died recently.

479
00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:17.690
I know.

480
00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:22.340
He's like, he did three weeks ago.

481
00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.180
Good, Angela.

482
00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:25.680
Okay, I have another improv moment for you.

483
00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:26.100
Okay.

484
00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:31.920
When Kevin sympathetically reaches across the table to hold Oscar's hand, that was not

485
00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:32.420
scripted.

486
00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:33.880
Brian improvised that.

487
00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:34.940
It was a nice touch.

488
00:22:34.940 --> 00:22:35.560
Wasn't it?

489
00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:38.780
I love that these little webisodes each have a button on the end.

490
00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.780
All right.

491
00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:41.380
Webisode number two.

492
00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:43.800
This one is titled Phyllis.

493
00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:49.540
In their search for the missing $3,000, the accountants are going to meet with Phyllis.

494
00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:55.280
Angela has a talking head where she says, Michael is the obvious suspect, but since he's

495
00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:58.940
the boss, they have to at least pretend to look at other people firSt.

496
00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:04.000
This begins the recap nature of the webisodes.

497
00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:10.480
You will notice, even though they all flow together, they also still had to stand alone,

498
00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:14.920
which meant every episode, someone had to recap the plot.

499
00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:16.740
Someone had to tell us.

500
00:23:16.980 --> 00:23:18.600
$3,000 is missing.

501
00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:20.840
And everyone is a suspect.

502
00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:23.260
In this one, it was your job, Ange.

503
00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:28.580
Well, Oscar's going to ask Phyllis if she bought anything with company money, and she looks

504
00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:29.160
down guilty.

505
00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:30.580
Angela's like, I knew it.

506
00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:36.840
Phyllis explains that she broke the heel on her shoe while at a corporate sales call.

507
00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:38.320
I just love that backstory.

508
00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:39.120
I know.

509
00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:39.820
