00:31:31.360 --> 00:31:33.440
I'm very, very excited to be back.

671
00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:37.360
And now to be talking to you guys about the Accountants.

672
00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:38.400
Here's my story.

673
00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:39.680
We're filming.

674
00:31:40.040 --> 00:31:41.760
No one else is on set.

675
00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:47.140
Me, you, Angela, and Oscar, we are recording.

676
00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:50.240
And I'm recording a talking head, a direct address to the camera.

677
00:31:50.460 --> 00:31:52.280
And we're in the annex.

678
00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:59.500
My back was to the room with the snacks and by Toby's desk.

679
00:31:59.980 --> 00:32:02.760
And I'm recording a talking head, and I'm talking to the camera.

680
00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:08.480
And just behind the camera, I see, as we're recording, Greg Daniels walked by.

681
00:32:08.900 --> 00:32:15.920
And I see my old friend from high school, Ed Helms, walked by the camera.

682
00:32:16.060 --> 00:32:24.760
Now, in that moment, I'm not thinking, oh, there's Ed Helms, star of The Daily Show, comedian and actor.

683
00:32:24.760 --> 00:32:26.920
My brain didn't go there.

684
00:32:27.100 --> 00:32:30.400
My brain went back to high school in Atlanta, Georgia.

685
00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:32.620
I was like, Ed Helms?

686
00:32:32.860 --> 00:32:38.500
Why is my old buddy Ed Helms on The Office set?

687
00:32:38.500 --> 00:32:42.120
But come to find out, he was there meeting with Greg.

688
00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:48.780
He had a deal with NBC, and he was meeting with Greg about joining The Office in season three.

689
00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:53.060
This was his, like, introductory meeting with Greg Daniels.

690
00:32:53.060 --> 00:32:59.480
So I saw him, gave him a hug, and remember saying so specifically, why are you here?

691
00:32:59.620 --> 00:33:03.120
Which, in retrospect, it was very embarrassing.

692
00:33:05.300 --> 00:33:06.780
That is so crazy.

693
00:33:07.040 --> 00:33:08.280
Isn't that so wild?

694
00:33:08.340 --> 00:33:09.900
And I totally hear that.

695
00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:12.460
You know when you see someone completely out of contact?

696
00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:12.880
Yes.

697
00:33:12.880 --> 00:33:14.540
And you can't connect the dots?

698
00:33:14.720 --> 00:33:14.960
Yes.

699
00:33:15.340 --> 00:33:20.060
I just thought that was so wild to see your old high school friend all of a sudden at your place of work.

700
00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:20.540
You're like, what?

701
00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:21.140
What's happening?

702
00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:27.800
Well, we also got several fan questions about Kevin's talking head, where he's talking about his IQ score.

703
00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:29.960
One is from Amelia S.

704
00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:35.960
in Akron, Ohio, who said, please do a breakdown deep dive on IQs or IQ tests.

705
00:33:36.340 --> 00:33:42.240
And Ivy from Canada said, Kevin says he scored over 100 on an IQ teSt.

706
00:33:42.240 --> 00:33:48.640
The average IQ in the world in the 1970s, estimating when he may have taken it, was 90.

707
00:33:49.380 --> 00:33:51.640
Average IQ has dropped over the years.

708
00:33:51.640 --> 00:33:54.200
It was 87 in 2024.

709
00:33:54.340 --> 00:33:59.500
But nonetheless, does this mean that Kevin had an above average IQ as a child?

710
00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:02.820
Well, you know I've never been so excited to deep dive something.

711
00:34:02.820 --> 00:34:07.540
I was going to say, I mean, this call to action from Amelia, you must have been like, hey.

712
00:34:08.260 --> 00:34:09.500
I was very excited.

713
00:34:09.500 --> 00:34:14.380
I was also very intrigued when Ivy said that IQ scores had been dropping.

714
00:34:14.660 --> 00:34:16.260
I had to know everything.

715
00:34:16.640 --> 00:34:16.720
Oh my, yes.

716
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:18.800
All right, here's what I found out.

717
00:34:18.900 --> 00:34:23.780
There are so many different IQ tests, and they all have different ways that they score.

718
00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:24.520
Okay.

719
00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:32.880
But in general, almost all of them say that 100 is like their median score.

720
00:34:33.360 --> 00:34:33.960
Oh.

721
00:34:34.140 --> 00:34:42.360
And so in general, a score of 85 to 114 signifies average intelligence.

722
00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:43.180
Okay.

723
00:34:43.460 --> 00:34:50.860
So what we've learned is that Kevin is of average intelligence, according to his reporting of his IQ score.

724
00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:53.100
Although Kevin thinks he's a genius.

725
00:34:53.100 --> 00:34:54.180
Yes, I guess so.

726
00:34:54.660 --> 00:35:01.920
If you have an IQ score of 115 to 129, you are above average or bright.

727
00:35:02.540 --> 00:35:07.660
If your score is 130 to 144, you are moderately gifted.

728
00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:12.740
145 to 159 is highly gifted.

729
00:35:12.740 --> 00:35:17.900
And it is estimated that Einstein's IQ was around 160.

730
00:35:18.640 --> 00:35:19.180
Dang.

731
00:35:19.640 --> 00:35:23.000
I love that that's my response to someone who's really smart.

732
00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:23.920
Like, dang.

733
00:35:24.580 --> 00:35:24.760
Dang.

734
00:35:25.220 --> 00:35:25.320
Dang.

735
00:35:25.320 --> 00:35:25.760
Shit.

736
00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.760
That's some impressive stuff.

737
00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:30.040
You go, Einstein.

738
00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:31.640
Einstein, I'm so proud of you.

739
00:35:32.820 --> 00:35:38.760
Well, about 98% of people have a score 130 or below.

740
00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:43.000
Only 2% of the population score above that.

741
00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:48.920
So only 2% of people are considered moderately to highly gifted.

742
00:35:49.920 --> 00:36:01.700
According to 2019's The Intelligence of the Nations report, the average IQ in the United States was 97.43.

743
00:36:02.020 --> 00:36:02.360
Uh-oh.

744
00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:03.220
Where is this leading?

745
00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:04.260
Where do we rank?

746
00:36:04.260 --> 00:36:06.120
We're doing well globally.

747
00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:06.600
Okay.

748
00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:08.440
There was a 2010 study.

749
00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:11.520
It took the scores of 108 nations.

750
00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:11.980
Okay.

751
00:36:12.120 --> 00:36:16.740
And found that the average IQ across that global sample was 89.

752
00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:17.620
Okay.

753
00:36:18.120 --> 00:36:24.200
Now, it's very important to note that these kinds of tests can be misinterpreted.

754
00:36:24.300 --> 00:36:26.300
They can be culturally biased.

755
00:36:26.960 --> 00:36:32.340
Different countries have different ideas of what intelligence is and how to measure it.

756
00:36:32.340 --> 00:36:42.340
But, in fact, IQ testing is sometimes considered controversial because intelligence measurements, they can be misinterpreted.

757
00:36:42.980 --> 00:36:47.320
They can be misused to stigmatize marginalized groups.

