00:46:57.420 --> 00:46:59.420
Kevin's like, well, you'd have to take it from petty cash.

1021
00:46:59.540 --> 00:47:01.100
Roy's like, I don't even know where you keep it.

1022
00:47:01.220 --> 00:47:02.480
Kevin says, in Oscar's drawer.

1023
00:47:02.940 --> 00:47:04.620
Roy says, well, isn't it locked?

1024
00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:06.520
Kevin goes, well, he keeps the key behind the counter.

1025
00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:10.360
And Oscar's like, Kevin, why are you telling him how to steal?

1026
00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:12.680
And Roy's like, no, I wouldn't do that.

1027
00:47:12.780 --> 00:47:13.260
It's wrong.

1028
00:47:13.400 --> 00:47:14.780
And Angela's like, well, I'm satisfied.

1029
00:47:15.020 --> 00:47:15.800
Thank you for your time.

1030
00:47:16.660 --> 00:47:19.020
And then Kevin says, Roy, one more question.

1031
00:47:19.280 --> 00:47:20.440
What do you think of Angela?

1032
00:47:21.180 --> 00:47:22.580
And I have an improv moment.

1033
00:47:22.580 --> 00:47:23.600
What was it?

1034
00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:26.520
When Oscar says, you don't have to answer that.

1035
00:47:26.640 --> 00:47:28.940
And Kevin says, but you can if you want to.

1036
00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:30.080
That was improv?

1037
00:47:30.460 --> 00:47:30.720
Yes.

1038
00:47:31.960 --> 00:47:33.300
I like that a lot.

1039
00:47:33.760 --> 00:47:34.280
All right.

1040
00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:37.240
Episode number six is titled The Memo.

1041
00:47:37.560 --> 00:47:43.220
At this point, the accountants have ruled out Phyllis, Stanley, Jim, Meredith, and themselves.

1042
00:47:44.300 --> 00:47:46.380
Although Angela isn't so sure about that.

1043
00:47:46.920 --> 00:47:49.880
Kevin has a talking head where he says he didn't steal it.

1044
00:47:49.880 --> 00:47:53.640
And Angela says she is positive it's not Dwight.

1045
00:47:53.800 --> 00:47:56.460
He has the most integrity of anyone in the office.

1046
00:47:57.200 --> 00:47:57.460
Yes.

1047
00:47:57.640 --> 00:47:59.020
And then they stare at her oddly.

1048
00:47:59.300 --> 00:48:03.540
So just a reminder, this was released between season two and season three.

1049
00:48:03.880 --> 00:48:10.440
So the audience knows that Dwight and Angela are a couple, but the people in the office will not find out until season five.

1050
00:48:10.840 --> 00:48:11.320
Yeah.

1051
00:48:11.600 --> 00:48:14.100
When Phyllis spills the beans in Moroccan Christmas.

1052
00:48:14.540 --> 00:48:14.720
Yeah.

1053
00:48:14.720 --> 00:48:18.520
So I loved that we sprinkled this in to the webisode.

1054
00:48:18.840 --> 00:48:22.580
Well, up next is one of my favorite lines of the accountants webisode series.

1055
00:48:22.840 --> 00:48:23.400
What is it?

1056
00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:25.880
Angela says to Oscar, did you talk to Kelly?

1057
00:48:26.180 --> 00:48:27.220
Oscar says, yes.

1058
00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:29.020
She told me she didn't do it.

1059
00:48:29.120 --> 00:48:31.840
And then 45 minutes later, the conversation ended.

1060
00:48:32.080 --> 00:48:32.940
Yes, that's right.

1061
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:39.320
And then Kevin says he talked to Creed and he didn't do it either, although he did offer to sell me some dietary supplements.

1062
00:48:39.920 --> 00:48:45.820
Well, they decide that they're going to write a memo, but first they're going to argue over who gets to write it.

1063
00:48:46.060 --> 00:48:46.500
That's right.

1064
00:48:46.640 --> 00:48:47.760
Angela says, I'll write it.

1065
00:48:47.880 --> 00:48:49.700
And then Kevin says, no, I want to write it.

1066
00:48:50.040 --> 00:48:53.160
And Kevin's like, come on, you never let me write accounting memos.

1067
00:48:53.320 --> 00:48:55.620
And Angela says, fine, but I'll supervise.

1068
00:48:56.100 --> 00:49:01.820
I want to point out that Kate, Leslie, and Phyllis are all in the background of this.

1069
00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:08.540
This is the most filled out this rest of this bullpen world has been in any of the webisode.

1070
00:49:08.540 --> 00:49:14.120
So I don't know what happened with everyone's schedule, but everyone was there at the same time for this scene.

1071
00:49:14.340 --> 00:49:14.720
For this one moment.

1072
00:49:14.960 --> 00:49:16.300
And Randall took advantage of it.

1073
00:49:16.540 --> 00:49:18.000
Well, I have an improv moment.

1074
00:49:18.220 --> 00:49:25.920
As we're leaving the conference room, I improvised shutting the door behind me, knowing that Kevin is right behind me and he'd almost walk into it.

1075
00:49:26.140 --> 00:49:35.220
I got so tickled rewatching this because if you go to that moment, you can hear Brian as Kevin say, God, because he is so annoyed.

1076
00:49:35.220 --> 00:49:40.280
And it makes me laugh every time because Brian and I would do stuff like this to each other.

1077
00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:40.800
You would.

1078
00:49:41.020 --> 00:49:44.740
When we were in scenes together, we like to like mess around with each other.

1079
00:49:44.820 --> 00:49:47.600
And he's really like the brother I never had.

1080
00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:49.500
And this was me just messing with him.

1081
00:49:49.920 --> 00:49:54.040
Well, now Kevin is typing the memo, but Angela is micromanaging him.

1082
00:49:54.180 --> 00:49:54.520
Yes.

1083
00:49:54.700 --> 00:49:55.340
Over his shoulder.

1084
00:49:55.520 --> 00:49:59.780
He clearly does not know what it means to make the date right justified.

1085
00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:00.480
Nope.

1086
00:50:00.960 --> 00:50:04.360
I mean, this is what we were just talking about before.

1087
00:50:04.860 --> 00:50:08.220
Now, like our computers write our memos for us.

1088
00:50:08.340 --> 00:50:11.640
We don't have to learn proper memo or letter writing.

1089
00:50:11.940 --> 00:50:12.860
Oh, yeah, for sure.

1090
00:50:12.960 --> 00:50:13.600
There's templates.

1091
00:50:13.860 --> 00:50:15.900
Like if you want to write a resume, there's a template.

1092
00:50:16.100 --> 00:50:16.900
You just fill it in.

1093
00:50:17.020 --> 00:50:18.780
I think we're getting dumber as a result.

1094
00:50:18.920 --> 00:50:19.560
I really do.

1095
00:50:19.740 --> 00:50:20.680
This is my complaint.

1096
00:50:21.000 --> 00:50:23.060
This is my soapbox about AI.

1097
00:50:23.720 --> 00:50:25.220
I don't think it's good.

1098
00:50:25.220 --> 00:50:29.040
I don't think it's good that it's writing our essays for us.

1099
00:50:29.160 --> 00:50:30.400
And I don't know.

1100
00:50:30.800 --> 00:50:33.200
You know how I feel about getting a new TV remote.

1101
00:50:34.020 --> 00:50:37.480
So just because it does more stuff doesn't mean it's better.

1102
00:50:37.660 --> 00:50:40.120
We're not less busy than we were before.

1103
00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:42.160
It's not saving us any time.

1104
00:50:42.240 --> 00:50:45.440
We're not spending more time on leisure activities.

1105
00:50:45.820 --> 00:50:47.180
And I think we should.

1106
00:50:47.440 --> 00:50:52.700
Well, it's because we have, you know, productivity culture in this country.

1107
00:50:52.700 --> 00:50:54.300
We value productivity.

1108
00:50:54.300 --> 00:50:56.900
I suffer from this same illness.

1109
00:50:57.340 --> 00:51:01.820
I don't often feel self-esteem unless I'm being productive.

1110
00:51:02.300 --> 00:51:03.380
It's a problem.

1111
00:51:04.100 --> 00:51:05.920
But it's affecting our health.

1112
00:51:06.280 --> 00:51:07.300
It is.

1113
00:51:07.660 --> 00:51:10.320
You know, Kendra writes about it in her book, The Plan.

1114
00:51:10.480 --> 00:51:12.180
And it really spoke to me, that section.

1115
00:51:12.540 --> 00:51:12.680
Yeah.

1116
00:51:12.940 --> 00:51:14.040
Always having a deadline.

1117
00:51:14.220 --> 00:51:15.320
Always pushing, pushing, pushing.

1118
00:51:15.700 --> 00:51:16.080
Yes.

1119
00:51:16.140 --> 00:51:19.220
And all of it is supposedly, quote, unquote, saving us time.

1120
00:51:19.220 --> 00:51:20.860
But we're all busier than we were.

1121
00:51:21.520 --> 00:51:22.240
All right.

1122
00:51:22.440 --> 00:51:23.240
Soapbox over.

1123
00:51:23.420 --> 00:51:23.620
Whatever.

1124
00:51:24.300 --> 00:51:26.620
I'm sure everyone agrees anyway.

1125
00:51:26.640 --> 00:51:28.920
I'm not saying any new thoughts here.

1126
00:51:29.100 --> 00:51:30.040
I like that you.

1127
00:51:30.180 --> 00:51:30.980
It's nothing groundbreaking.

1128
00:51:30.980 --> 00:51:35.660
I love it when you end a soapbox with just like, you're just so, whatever.

1129
00:51:36.480 --> 00:51:37.280
Soapbox over.

1130
00:51:37.280 --> 00:51:42.740
I mean, I get fired up, but then I'm also like, well, I don't know.

1131
00:51:44.240 --> 00:51:45.720
I'm also tired.

1132
00:51:46.120 --> 00:51:47.120
You're also just tired.

1133
00:51:48.780 --> 00:51:51.080
Well, Kevin is going to finish his own memo.

1134
00:51:51.640 --> 00:51:53.340
He wrote Angela stinks.

1135
00:51:54.460 --> 00:51:56.300
He says he's not going to hand it out.

1136
00:51:56.300 --> 00:51:57.080
It's just for him.

1137
00:51:57.220 --> 00:51:57.280
It's just for him.

1138
00:51:57.280 --> 00:51:59.580
In fact, forget, actually, I said anything about it.

1139
00:51:59.620 --> 00:52:00.460
Oh, God, what have I done?

1140
00:52:00.640 --> 00:52:01.100
Oh, my gosh.

1141
00:52:01.120 --> 00:52:01.880
It's so funny.

1142
00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:03.720
He totally spirals.

1143
00:52:03.840 --> 00:52:05.560
He's so tickled with himself.

1144
00:52:05.660 --> 00:52:06.380
His progression.

1145
00:52:06.780 --> 00:52:07.980
And then he's like, wait, hold on.

1146
00:52:08.680 --> 00:52:09.660
Don't show her that.

1147
00:52:10.960 --> 00:52:11.560
All right.

1148
00:52:11.560 --> 00:52:14.300
Episode number seven, things are getting tense.

1149
00:52:15.100 --> 00:52:16.720
This is my personal favorite.

1150
00:52:17.560 --> 00:52:22.280
Well, as the search for the missing money continues, the accountants start to turn on one another.

1151
00:52:22.480 --> 00:52:24.680
We start this over in accounting again.

1152
00:52:24.900 --> 00:52:26.440
Everyone is seated at their desk.

1153
00:52:26.440 --> 00:52:27.760
They're working on something.

1154
00:52:28.320 --> 00:52:30.780
I have a SAS catch for you.

1155
00:52:30.920 --> 00:52:31.500
What is it?

1156
00:52:31.640 --> 00:52:35.500
At 13 seconds, you can see my SAS shoes as I sit at my desk.

1157
00:52:36.220 --> 00:52:40.900
These were the early days of the office, and those are my classic season one SAS shoes.

1158
00:52:41.320 --> 00:52:44.520
And I'd also like to point out a southern accent catch.

1159
00:52:44.760 --> 00:52:45.580
What is it?

1160
00:52:45.860 --> 00:52:51.040
Angela's Talking Head, when she says, we are missing $3,000, things are getting tense.

1161
00:52:51.560 --> 00:52:52.980
Things are getting tense.

1162
00:52:53.640 --> 00:52:55.160
Your recap Talking Head?

1163
00:52:55.340 --> 00:52:55.680
Mm-hmm.

1164
00:52:56.000 --> 00:53:01.240
You had to do a lot of those, like different versions of recapping the plot for us.

1165
00:53:01.300 --> 00:53:01.740
I did.

1166
00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:03.780
But things weren't tense.

1167
00:53:03.780 --> 00:53:04.520
They were tense.

1168
00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:05.300
They were tense.

1169
00:53:06.580 --> 00:53:08.080
I just loved this one.

1170
00:53:08.260 --> 00:53:09.180
This is my favorite.

1171
00:53:09.180 --> 00:53:10.120
Number seven.

1172
00:53:10.900 --> 00:53:14.180
I just thought it was such great accounting chemistry.

1173
00:53:14.740 --> 00:53:19.000
I love that we find out that Kevin once gambled with petty cash.

1174
00:53:19.180 --> 00:53:19.340
Yeah.

1175
00:53:19.600 --> 00:53:20.320
$2,800.

1176
00:53:21.140 --> 00:53:21.520
Yes.

1177
00:53:21.760 --> 00:53:25.720
I love that Angela's wearing a new necklace and everyone notices.

1178
00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:27.720
And clearly, it's from Dwight.

1179
00:53:27.840 --> 00:53:28.560
Well-

1180
00:53:28.560 --> 00:53:29.380
But she won't say.

1181
00:53:29.500 --> 00:53:30.440
She won't say.

1182
00:53:30.600 --> 00:53:33.320
Although she's very much self-consciously fidgeting with it.

1183
00:53:33.320 --> 00:53:38.400
I wanted to tell you guys, in the script, it said that Angela's friend's name was Diane

1184
00:53:38.400 --> 00:53:39.780
Chester Berg.

1185
00:53:40.400 --> 00:53:43.520
And in one take, I changed the last name.

1186
00:53:43.640 --> 00:53:45.960
I said Diane Chester Schneberg.

1187
00:53:46.300 --> 00:53:49.520
And I liked that because it was clearly Angela lying.

1188
00:53:49.740 --> 00:53:54.500
She was clearly trying to cover up Dwight Kurt Schroet with Diane Chester Schneberg.

1189
00:53:54.500 --> 00:54:01.940
One of my all-time favorite comedy things is when someone says a fakie name to try to lie

1190
00:54:01.940 --> 00:54:03.100
their way out of something.

1191
00:54:03.420 --> 00:54:04.740
And they can't.

1192
00:54:04.880 --> 00:54:08.920
I think it's because I am not good at improv on the spot.

1193
00:54:08.920 --> 00:54:16.080
And whenever I was in improv classes and I had to like say my character name, it was always

1194
00:54:16.080 --> 00:54:17.100
stupid like that.

1195
00:54:17.100 --> 00:54:18.760
It was never clever.

1196
00:54:18.960 --> 00:54:21.160
It was always just mangled things.

1197
00:54:21.160 --> 00:54:23.400
Oh, can we all go around and do one?

1198
00:54:23.560 --> 00:54:25.700
Can we all say a fakie character name?

1199
00:54:25.840 --> 00:54:26.260
Sure.

1200
00:54:27.200 --> 00:54:28.380
Mine's going to be awful.

1201
00:54:29.060 --> 00:54:29.560
All right.

1202
00:54:29.600 --> 00:54:30.300
Who goes first?

1203
00:54:30.500 --> 00:54:31.920
Make up a fakie character name.

1204
00:54:32.080 --> 00:54:32.600
Sam, go.

1205
00:54:33.580 --> 00:54:34.440
Smithers Crampton.

1206
00:54:34.940 --> 00:54:36.620
You did that so quickly.

1207
00:54:36.880 --> 00:54:37.160
Thank you.

1208
00:54:37.280 --> 00:54:38.580
You're Smithers Crampton?

1209
00:54:38.760 --> 00:54:39.280
That's good.

1210
00:54:39.280 --> 00:54:40.240
I like that character.

1211
00:54:40.240 --> 00:54:41.720
I have an idea of him in my head.

1212
00:54:41.900 --> 00:54:42.100
Okay.

1213
00:54:42.700 --> 00:54:42.940
Yeah.

1214
00:54:43.120 --> 00:54:44.960
Smithers is friends with Ted Bungus.

1215
00:54:45.240 --> 00:54:46.280
Ted Bungus.

1216
00:54:46.480 --> 00:54:46.800
Okay.

1217
00:54:47.100 --> 00:54:47.780
All right.

1218
00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:51.660
I am Betsy Belly Welly.

1219
00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:52.520
See?

1220
00:54:52.860 --> 00:54:53.680
No, but that's it.

1221
00:54:53.820 --> 00:54:54.720
Betsy Belly Welly.

1222
00:54:54.800 --> 00:54:58.160
But I say it like I started off so strong.

1223
00:54:58.340 --> 00:54:59.940
That was not even me doing a bit.

1224
00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:03.320
That was me really panicking in the middle of saying a name.

1225
00:55:03.460 --> 00:55:06.520
Well, this is exactly what Angela Martin did.

1226
00:55:06.520 --> 00:55:07.300
Who is this woman?

1227
00:55:07.580 --> 00:55:11.240
She, she, that's, that's exactly the acting lesson.

1228
00:55:12.040 --> 00:55:13.060
Angela, what's yours?

1229
00:55:13.220 --> 00:55:13.360
Go.

1230
00:55:14.980 --> 00:55:16.020
Tilda Nels.

1231
00:55:16.530 --> 00:55:17.380
Tilda Nels.

1232
00:55:17.600 --> 00:55:18.600
Tilda Nels.

1233
00:55:19.940 --> 00:55:20.720
Okay.

1234
00:55:21.280 --> 00:55:22.120
All right.

1235
00:55:22.240 --> 00:55:25.320
I'd love to read a script, a short.

1236
00:55:25.580 --> 00:55:26.260
Of those?

1237
00:55:26.480 --> 00:55:27.520
Of those four characters.

1238
00:55:28.700 --> 00:55:30.520
That would be great, actually.

1239
00:55:31.100 --> 00:55:31.660
Okay.

1240
00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:37.500
Well, as the accountants just go back and forth at one another, Kevin's like, we have to stop

1241
00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:37.720
this.

1242
00:55:37.780 --> 00:55:39.260
We can't start turning on one another.

1243
00:55:39.380 --> 00:55:41.560
That's what the guy who sold the money would want us to do.

1244
00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.840
The only thing left to do is to investigate Michael.

1245
00:55:45.380 --> 00:55:49.560
And then the camera pans over and we see someone at Michael's desk.

1246
00:55:49.700 --> 00:55:50.300
Who is it?

1247
00:55:50.500 --> 00:55:51.520
It's not Steve.

1248
00:55:51.740 --> 00:55:52.820
It's not Steve.

1249
00:55:53.100 --> 00:55:57.700
And we're going to see a lot of this person in the next episode, number eight, titled You're

1250
00:55:57.700 --> 00:55:58.060
Mean.

1251
00:55:58.060 --> 00:56:00.500
And we got a lot of fan questions about it.

1252
00:56:00.800 --> 00:56:01.480
So who is it?

1253
00:56:01.880 --> 00:56:02.740
Well, Amelia S.

1254
00:56:02.840 --> 00:56:06.720
from Akron, Ohio said, I noticed all the shots of Michael are from across the

1255
00:56:06.720 --> 00:56:08.120
bullpen, far away.

1256
00:56:09.540 --> 00:56:10.680
And Becky K.

1257
00:56:10.880 --> 00:56:13.760
from Katy, Texas said, who was the actor who played Michael?

1258
00:56:13.760 --> 00:56:16.160
I assume it was not Steve Carell.

1259
00:56:16.540 --> 00:56:20.460
Well, everyone, it was a photo double played by Paul Bunnell.

1260
00:56:21.140 --> 00:56:25.320
And Angela, of course, you knew it wasn't Steve Carell because you were there.

1261
00:56:25.500 --> 00:56:25.980
That's right.

1262
00:56:26.180 --> 00:56:28.420
I love that it sold that moment, though.

1263
00:56:28.640 --> 00:56:29.900
It really helped.

1264
00:56:30.060 --> 00:56:36.740
Although Becky did say, I thought it was weird that Michael didn't have a big goodbye when

1265
00:56:36.740 --> 00:56:37.820
he leaves the office.

1266
00:56:37.820 --> 00:56:45.120
Because the top of this next webisode is going to begin with Michael leaving.

1267
00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:51.000
And this makes it possible for the accountants to go into his office and start poking around.

1268
00:56:51.700 --> 00:56:55.700
But before they go into Michael's office, they're kind of on a stakeout.

1269
00:56:55.920 --> 00:56:57.400
They're just waiting for Michael to leave.

1270
00:56:57.980 --> 00:56:59.520
Kevin says, what time is it?

1271
00:56:59.600 --> 00:57:00.560
Like, why hasn't he gone?

1272
00:57:00.680 --> 00:57:01.520
What time is it?

1273
00:57:01.680 --> 00:57:05.360
And Angela says, why don't you check the clock for yourself?

1274
00:57:05.360 --> 00:57:08.280
And he's like, why don't you just tell me what time it is?

1275
00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:10.500
And she's like, I think people should be self-sufficient.

1276
00:57:10.980 --> 00:57:12.480
Well, Kevin thinks she's mean.

1277
00:57:13.240 --> 00:57:15.220
This really ruffles her feathers.

1278
00:57:15.360 --> 00:57:17.940
In the script, it says Angela makes busy work.

1279
00:57:18.620 --> 00:57:21.600
And then Kevin and Oscar sort of have this conversation.

1280
00:57:21.860 --> 00:57:24.960
Oscar's going to the mall because he needs a new walk.

1281
00:57:25.120 --> 00:57:28.060
And then Angela just blurts out, you know, I'm not mean.

1282
00:57:28.060 --> 00:57:36.760
Oh, lady, I have an audio clip because for whatever reason, Angela is going to apologize.

1283
00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:42.560
She's going to say sorry twice, not once, but twice.

1284
00:57:42.580 --> 00:57:47.840
And I thought we had to hear it because I'm fairly certain these are the only times the words

1285
00:57:47.840 --> 00:57:50.920
I'm sorry come out of Angela Martin's mouth ever.

1286
00:57:51.640 --> 00:57:53.580
I'm sorry if I was mean.

1287
00:57:57.530 --> 00:57:58.210
It's okay.

1288
00:57:59.070 --> 00:57:59.810
Thank you.

1289
00:58:04.420 --> 00:58:06.360
That was uncomfortable.

1290
00:58:11.150 --> 00:58:11.990
Okay, let's go.

1291
00:58:12.170 --> 00:58:13.310
This is so much fun.

1292
00:58:13.530 --> 00:58:14.830
It's not supposed to be fun.

1293
00:58:16.530 --> 00:58:18.030
Again, sorry.

1294
00:58:19.550 --> 00:58:20.510
Two sorries.

1295
00:58:20.730 --> 00:58:21.350
I know.

1296
00:58:22.030 --> 00:58:22.510
Wow.

1297
00:58:22.710 --> 00:58:23.170
I know.

1298
00:58:23.370 --> 00:58:27.270
I guess she clearly cares about Kevin thinking if she's mean or not.

1299
00:58:27.370 --> 00:58:28.810
In the webisodes, she does.

1300
00:58:28.930 --> 00:58:30.070
At least in this world.

1301
00:58:30.610 --> 00:58:32.770
But it's not going to stop her from being mean.

1302
00:58:32.770 --> 00:58:40.650
Well, as they walk over to Michael's office, Kevin does this very funny sort of dance move

1303
00:58:40.650 --> 00:58:42.190
towards Michael's office.

1304
00:58:42.430 --> 00:58:48.130
In the script, it says, Kevin does the Jim Belushi slash Animal House entering the dean's

1305
00:58:48.130 --> 00:58:49.390
office stealth maneuver.

1306
00:58:49.390 --> 00:58:51.990
Yes, it was lost on me.

1307
00:58:52.110 --> 00:58:54.450
It's also lost on Angela and Oscar.

1308
00:58:54.970 --> 00:58:55.270
Yes.

1309
00:58:55.390 --> 00:58:58.310
In the script, it didn't give any stage direction for our reaction.

1310
00:58:58.310 --> 00:59:01.170
But Oscar and I both just chose to be not impressed.

1311
00:59:01.610 --> 00:59:03.430
And Brian improvised.

1312
00:59:03.590 --> 00:59:05.230
You guys are breaking my spirit.

1313
00:59:07.230 --> 00:59:10.490
All right, episode number nine, titled Michael's office.

1314
00:59:10.810 --> 00:59:11.630
They are in there.

1315
00:59:11.870 --> 00:59:13.890
They are looking through his stuff.

1316
00:59:14.230 --> 00:59:15.510
This is my favorite one.

1317
00:59:15.690 --> 00:59:16.750
This is your favorite?

1318
00:59:16.750 --> 00:59:21.410
Yes, because we just were sort of just doing all of these silly bits.

1319
00:59:21.710 --> 00:59:26.450
And, you know, Kevin has the first line in the webisode, but it wasn't scripted for him

1320
00:59:26.450 --> 00:59:28.710
to say it into Michael's toy megaphone.

1321
00:59:28.810 --> 00:59:30.010
I thought that was so funny.

1322
00:59:30.170 --> 00:59:31.310
Brian just did that.

1323
00:59:31.310 --> 00:59:32.370
I loved it.

1324
00:59:32.510 --> 00:59:34.150
He also added the attention.

1325
00:59:34.150 --> 00:59:34.550
Yes.

1326
00:59:35.530 --> 00:59:39.670
Now, the part where he picks up the train whistle and blows it, that was scripted?

1327
00:59:39.670 --> 00:59:40.730
That was, yes.

1328
00:59:41.070 --> 00:59:46.130
I love that Oscar points out the Seiko timepiece, like, certificate.

1329
00:59:46.130 --> 00:59:47.630
I just loved that.

1330
00:59:47.770 --> 00:59:48.090
Yes.

1331
00:59:48.390 --> 00:59:50.910
And then something odd happens.

1332
00:59:51.250 --> 00:59:59.370
They unlock a drawer in Michael's office, and they find nine Dunder Mifflin snow globes.

1333
00:59:59.830 --> 01:00:02.030
It's so interesting.

1334
01:00:02.450 --> 01:00:03.090
Why?

1335
01:00:03.090 --> 01:00:04.330
Like, why?

1336
01:00:04.650 --> 01:00:05.790
What are those for?

1337
01:00:06.050 --> 01:00:06.850
I don't know.

1338
01:00:07.950 --> 01:00:11.610
And Kevin says if he had a snow globe drawer, he'd keep it locked, too.

1339
01:00:11.870 --> 01:00:12.110
Yeah.

1340
01:00:13.030 --> 01:00:15.330
Well, Oscar tells Angela to go online.

1341
01:00:15.550 --> 01:00:16.850
Look at Michael's Quicken.

1342
01:00:17.470 --> 01:00:20.150
I have a little thing to share about this.

1343
01:00:20.290 --> 01:00:21.870
The scene was actually longer.

1344
01:00:22.070 --> 01:00:22.390
Okay.

1345
01:00:22.530 --> 01:00:25.690
When Angela logged onto the computer, it started like this.

1346
01:00:26.030 --> 01:00:27.710
Angela says, okay, I'm in.

1347
01:00:27.970 --> 01:00:28.990
Ugh, gross.

1348
01:00:29.470 --> 01:00:30.670
Oscar and Kevin look.

1349
01:00:30.930 --> 01:00:32.170
Kevin says, oh, my God.

1350
01:00:32.530 --> 01:00:33.930
Oscar says, yikes.

1351
01:00:34.190 --> 01:00:37.090
Kevin says, that guy must be like 100 years old.

1352
01:00:37.430 --> 01:00:39.190
Oscar says, what's he holding?

1353
01:00:39.950 --> 01:00:41.950
Kevin says, I think it's a shovel.

1354
01:00:42.590 --> 01:00:45.350
And then Oscar says, okay, okay, go check his Quicken files.

1355
01:00:46.010 --> 01:00:49.190
What in the world had come up on the computer?

1356
01:00:49.350 --> 01:00:50.450
What was he Googling?

1357
01:00:50.450 --> 01:00:51.850
I don't know.

1358
01:00:52.690 --> 01:00:57.430
The last eight charges were from Jack's Joke and Magic Shop.

1359
01:00:57.630 --> 01:00:58.730
He loves that place.

1360
01:00:59.470 --> 01:01:02.130
Angela's going to go ahead and pay his electric bill real quickly.

1361
01:01:02.350 --> 01:01:04.390
This was my favorite thing that I did.

1362
01:01:04.630 --> 01:01:06.390
It was so fun to me.

1363
01:01:06.810 --> 01:01:08.510
And when Kevin's like, what are you doing?

1364
01:01:08.570 --> 01:01:09.510
I'm like, I'm paying his electric.

1365
01:01:09.630 --> 01:01:10.850
It's about to be shut off.

1366
01:01:11.110 --> 01:01:14.830
Well, all of this snooping leads nowhere.

1367
01:01:15.290 --> 01:01:16.530
They don't find anything.

1368
01:01:16.750 --> 01:01:18.730
But Angela does pay some of Michael's bills.

1369
01:01:18.970 --> 01:01:19.270
Yes.

1370
01:01:19.270 --> 01:01:21.750
Well, we've made it now to the last one.

1371
01:01:21.910 --> 01:01:24.850
It's episode 10 titled, The Best Day of My Life.

1372
01:01:25.410 --> 01:01:27.610
It's going to start with Angela and Dwight.

1373
01:01:27.610 --> 01:01:29.210
They're whispering in the kitchen.

1374
01:01:29.710 --> 01:01:34.170
I really feel like these scenes help the writers see Rain and Ice chemistry.

1375
01:01:35.150 --> 01:01:35.690
Yes.

1376
01:01:35.950 --> 01:01:38.070
I wanted to play the clip from the scene.

1377
01:01:38.490 --> 01:01:40.310
Rain improvised a moment at the end.

1378
01:01:40.430 --> 01:01:41.430
Let's see if you can guess.

1379
01:01:42.290 --> 01:01:45.690
You're saying Michael stole money from his own company?

1380
01:01:46.130 --> 01:01:48.010
Well, we've asked everyone else.

1381
01:01:48.550 --> 01:01:48.970
No.

1382
01:01:49.430 --> 01:01:49.870
No.

1383
01:01:50.150 --> 01:01:50.830
That's insane.

1384
01:01:51.050 --> 01:01:51.990
It has to be somebody else.

1385
01:01:52.450 --> 01:01:53.250
Like Meredith.

1386
01:01:54.550 --> 01:01:55.430
Her creed.

1387
01:01:56.490 --> 01:01:57.390
No, Meredith.

1388
01:01:57.590 --> 01:01:57.890
Definitely.

1389
01:01:58.510 --> 01:01:59.290
We asked her.

1390
01:01:59.470 --> 01:02:00.650
She said she didn't do it.

1391
01:02:00.890 --> 01:02:03.330
Which is exactly what you'd say if you did do it.

1392
01:02:03.730 --> 01:02:04.470
Oh, man.

1393
01:02:04.550 --> 01:02:06.670
I should have been handling this investigation from the beginning.

1394
01:02:06.670 --> 01:02:08.650
I believe she didn't do it.

1395
01:02:09.190 --> 01:02:09.270
I believe she didn't do it.

1396
01:02:09.270 --> 01:02:09.950
Are you doubting me?

1397
01:02:12.270 --> 01:02:12.790
No.

1398
01:02:15.410 --> 01:02:16.370
And here.

1399
01:02:18.490 --> 01:02:19.550
Oh, my God.

1400
01:02:19.890 --> 01:02:21.490
There has to be a better explanation.

1401
01:02:21.490 --> 01:02:24.570
How did he afford that new water bet he's always bragging about?

1402
01:02:24.830 --> 01:02:25.470
He charged it.

1403
01:02:25.910 --> 01:02:26.250
Discover.

1404
01:02:26.530 --> 01:02:27.790
Made a little cash back on the deal.

1405
01:02:27.970 --> 01:02:28.430
Smart.

1406
01:02:28.930 --> 01:02:37.470
If you were a general in the army and you accused him without proof, you would be court-martialed in front of a firing squad.

1407
01:02:38.310 --> 01:02:39.150
That's not true.

1408
01:02:39.930 --> 01:02:40.270
Okay.

1409
01:02:40.530 --> 01:02:42.670
Watch A Few Good Men and tell me that that's not true.

1410
01:02:43.590 --> 01:02:45.650
I own it on DVD if you want to come by later.

1411
01:02:45.870 --> 01:02:46.990
You can't handle the truth.

1412
01:02:47.170 --> 01:02:47.670
Just kidding.

1413
01:02:47.850 --> 01:02:48.450
You can't.

1414
01:02:49.090 --> 01:02:55.150
I mean, I'm assuming it's the little bit about A Few Good Men.

1415
01:02:55.370 --> 01:02:58.530
It's just the very end when he says, you can't handle the truth.

1416
01:02:58.690 --> 01:02:59.030
Just kidding.

1417
01:02:59.130 --> 01:02:59.510
Yes, you can.

1418
01:03:03.980 --> 01:03:06.060
I love early Dwight and Angela.

1419
01:03:06.300 --> 01:03:08.700
It just is so fun to rewatch that.

1420
01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:12.100
Well, now, guess what?

1421
01:03:13.080 --> 01:03:14.740
Mystery is about to be solved.

1422
01:03:15.020 --> 01:03:15.980
Guess who it was.

1423
01:03:16.100 --> 01:03:17.900
Guess who it was.

1424
01:03:17.900 --> 01:03:21.420
From the very beginning, Jan said, I'm sure it's an accounting error.

1425
01:03:21.580 --> 01:03:25.280
And Angela says, it is not an accounting error, at least not mine.

1426
01:03:26.360 --> 01:03:27.440
Turns out it was.

1427
01:03:27.660 --> 01:03:28.180
Turns out it was.

1428
01:03:29.040 --> 01:03:31.580
She accidentally logged something twice.

1429
01:03:32.240 --> 01:03:32.540
Yep.

1430
01:03:33.500 --> 01:03:33.980
Yeah.

1431
01:03:34.400 --> 01:03:35.360
Case closed.

1432
01:03:36.180 --> 01:03:36.380
Yeah.

1433
01:03:36.520 --> 01:03:37.720
Angela's like, oh, well, there you go.

1434
01:03:37.860 --> 01:03:42.580
She is not going to even for one moment admit that she really screwed up.

1435
01:03:43.040 --> 01:03:44.700
She's back to business as usual.

1436
01:03:44.700 --> 01:03:48.420
But Kevin is really having a moment here.

1437
01:03:48.600 --> 01:03:50.920
He says, this is the best day of my life.

1438
01:03:51.360 --> 01:03:51.540
Yes.

1439
01:03:51.720 --> 01:03:52.660
Angela was wrong.

1440
01:03:52.940 --> 01:03:53.120
Yeah.

1441
01:03:53.320 --> 01:03:54.280
Angela did it.

1442
01:03:54.480 --> 01:03:59.860
His face as Angela realizes it, the smile that comes over his face and Oscar too.

1443
01:04:00.440 --> 01:04:02.860
They're going to live off this moment for a long time.

1444
01:04:03.020 --> 01:04:03.720
They sure are.

1445
01:04:04.460 --> 01:04:05.080
All right.

1446
01:04:05.220 --> 01:04:06.780
Well, there you have it, folks.

1447
